---

<section class="comparison-section comparison-product-summary" aria-labelledby="what-is-skedular-title">
  <h2 id="what-is-skedular-title">What is Skedular?</h2>
  {
    isGable || isRobin || isOfficely || isEnvoy || isKadence || isArchie || isDiskbird ? (
      <p>
        Skedular is a workspace platform for organizations managing private workplaces and operators running coworking, flexible workspace, and
        commercial workspace businesses. It combines workplace booking, coworking operations, subscriptions, billing, invoicing, marketplace
        publishing, workspace discovery, and enterprise integrations in a single platform.
      </p>
    ) : (
      <p>
        Skedular is a workspace platform for organizations managing private workplaces and operators running commercial workspace businesses. It
        supports workplace booking, workplace management, coworking operations, billing, subscriptions, marketplace discovery, and integrations.
      </p>
    )
  }
  <p>
    The platform is designed for organizations and workspace operators that need workplace booking, coworking operations, memberships, payments,
    invoicing, subscriptions, and public workspace workflows from a single system.
  </p>
</section>

{
  competitor && (
    <section class="comparison-section comparison-product-summary" aria-labelledby="what-is-competitor-title">
      <h2 id="what-is-competitor-title">What is {competitor.name}?</h2>
      {isSkedda ? (
        <>
          <p>
            Skedda is a workplace booking platform focused on desk booking, meeting room booking, interactive floor plans, resource scheduling,
            visitor management, and workplace coordination. It is commonly used by organizations, shared workplaces, and coworking operators that need
            a focused booking experience with strong governance, permissions, scheduling controls, and collaboration integrations.
          </p>
          <p>
            Skedda's strengths include interactive floor plans, booking rules, resource permissions, desk and room reservations, utilization
            analytics, Microsoft 365 and Google Workspace integrations, Slack, Microsoft Teams, SSO, and visitor management.
          </p>
        </>
      ) : isOfficeRnD ? (
        <>
          <p>OfficeRnD provides software for both workplace management and flexible workspace operations.</p>
          <p>
            Its Workplace product focuses on hybrid work, desk booking, room booking, workplace coordination, office utilization, visitor management,
            analytics, and employee workplace experience.
          </p>
          <p>
            Its Flex product focuses on coworking and flexible workspace operations, including memberships, billing, invoicing, subscriptions, member
            management, resource management, and workspace administration.
          </p>
          <p>
            OfficeRnD is commonly used by enterprises managing hybrid workplaces and by coworking operators running flexible workspace businesses.
          </p>
        </>
      ) : isNexudus ? (
        <>
          <p>
            Nexudus is a coworking and flexible workspace management platform designed for operators managing shared workspaces, serviced offices, and
            flexible work environments.
          </p>
          <p>
            The platform includes desk booking, meeting room booking, resource management, member management, billing, invoicing, memberships,
            payments, visitor management, community management, and operational workflows for workspace operators.
          </p>
          <p>
            Nexudus is commonly used by coworking operators that need detailed member administration, recurring billing, invoicing, booking
            management, and workspace operations in a single system.
          </p>
        </>
      ) : isGable ? (
        <>
          <p>
            Gable is a workplace platform focused on hybrid work, office management, and access to distributed workspaces. Rather than operating as a
            coworking management platform, Gable helps organizations manage workplace attendance, office operations, workspace access, visitor
            workflows, and employee access to a network of workspaces.
          </p>
          <p>
            The platform combines workplace booking, hybrid work coordination, visitor management, workplace analytics, workspace discovery, employee
            workplace benefits, and access to third-party workspace providers.
          </p>
          <p>
            Gable is commonly used by organizations supporting distributed teams that need flexible access to workspaces across multiple locations
            while maintaining workplace coordination and visibility.
          </p>
        </>
      ) : isRobin ? (
        <>
          <p>
            Robin is a workplace management platform focused on hybrid work, office coordination, desk booking, meeting room scheduling, workplace
            analytics, and employee workplace experience.
          </p>
          <p>
            The platform helps organizations coordinate when employees come into the office, manage workplace capacity, reserve desks and rooms,
            analyze office utilization, and improve workplace planning.
          </p>
          <p>
            Robin is commonly used by enterprises adopting hybrid work models and organizations focused on workplace experience, office attendance,
            and workplace analytics.
          </p>
        </>
      ) : isOfficely ? (
        <>
          <p>
            Officely is a workplace management platform designed for organizations running hybrid work environments. The platform is built around
            Slack and helps teams coordinate office attendance, reserve desks, book meeting rooms, manage workplace capacity, and improve office
            visibility.
          </p>
          <p>
            Officely is commonly used by organizations that already rely heavily on Slack and want workplace booking and office coordination workflows
            to happen directly inside the tools employees already use.
          </p>
          <p>
            Its strengths include Slack-native workflows, desk booking, workplace coordination, office attendance visibility, and lightweight hybrid
            workplace management.
          </p>
        </>
      ) : isEnvoy ? (
        <>
          <p>
            Envoy is a workplace management platform focused on visitor management, workplace coordination, workplace security, desk booking, room
            booking, and workplace experience.
          </p>
          <p>
            The platform helps organizations manage visitors, coordinate office attendance, reserve desks and meeting rooms, handle workplace
            deliveries, improve office operations, and provide a better workplace experience for employees and guests.
          </p>
          <p>
            Envoy is commonly used by enterprises that want strong visitor management capabilities alongside workplace booking and workplace
            coordination tools.
          </p>
        </>
      ) : isKadence ? (
        <>
          <p>
            Kadence is a workplace management platform focused on hybrid work, workplace coordination, desk booking, room booking, office attendance
            planning, workplace analytics, and space utilization.
          </p>
          <p>
            The platform helps organizations coordinate when employees come into the office, manage desk and room reservations, improve workplace
            visibility, and understand how office space is being used.
          </p>
          <p>
            Kadence is commonly used by organizations adopting hybrid work models that need workplace booking, attendance coordination, workplace
            analytics, and office utilization reporting.
          </p>
        </>
      ) : isArchie ? (
        <>
          <p>
            Archie is a coworking and flexible workspace management platform designed for coworking operators, shared offices, and flexible workspace
            providers.
          </p>
          <p>
            The platform combines member management, desk booking, room booking, invoicing, billing, contracts, payments, subscriptions, and workspace
            operations in a single system.
          </p>
          <p>
            Archie is commonly used by coworking operators that need memberships, recurring billing, workspace reservations, and day-to-day coworking
            administration.
          </p>
        </>
      ) : isDiskbird ? (
        <>
          <p>
            deskbird is a workplace management platform focused on hybrid work, desk booking, room booking, office attendance coordination, workplace
            visibility, and workplace analytics.
          </p>
          <p>
            The platform helps organizations coordinate office attendance, manage workplace capacity, reserve desks and meeting rooms, and improve
            visibility into how office space is used.
          </p>
          <p>
            deskbird is commonly used by organizations adopting hybrid work models that need workplace booking, attendance coordination, workplace
            analytics, and employee workplace experience capabilities.
          </p>
        </>
      ) : (
        <>
          <p>{competitor.summary}</p>
          <p>
            It is typically a fit for {competitor.bestFor.toLowerCase()}. Its main strengths include {competitor.strengths.join(", ").toLowerCase()}.
          </p>
        </>
      )}
    </section>
  )
}

<section class="comparison-section" aria-labelledby="feature-comparison-title">
  <h2 id="feature-comparison-title">Feature comparison</h2>
  {
    isSkedda ? (
      <p>
        Both platforms support workplace booking, desk booking, room booking, floor plans, permissions, and enterprise integrations. The main
        difference is scope. Skedda is strongest as a workplace booking and space management platform, while Skedular extends further into coworking
        operations, workspace commerce, subscriptions, billing, invoicing, marketplace publishing, and public workspace discovery.
      </p>
    ) : isOfficeRnD ? (
      <p>
        Both platforms support workplace booking, room booking, floor plans, permissions, coworking operations, billing, invoicing, subscriptions,
        payments, and enterprise identity. The main difference is product scope and intended workflow, especially around public workspace discovery
        and marketplace publishing.
      </p>
    ) : isNexudus ? (
      <p>
        Both platforms support workplace booking, coworking operations, memberships, billing, invoicing, payments, and workspace administration. The
        biggest differences are around marketplace publishing, public workspace discovery, and how each platform approaches workspace commerce.
      </p>
    ) : isGable ? (
      <p>
        Both platforms support workplace booking and flexible workspace access, but they approach the problem differently. Gable focuses on helping
        organizations access and coordinate distributed workspaces, while Skedular combines workplace booking, coworking operations, workspace
        commerce, subscriptions, billing, marketplace publishing, and workspace discovery.
      </p>
    ) : isRobin ? (
      <p>
        Both platforms support workplace booking and workplace management workflows. The biggest differences are that Robin focuses on hybrid
        workplace coordination and workplace experience, while Skedular extends into coworking operations, subscriptions, billing, invoicing,
        marketplace publishing, and workspace discovery.
      </p>
    ) : isOfficely ? (
      <p>
        Both platforms support workplace booking and workplace management workflows. The biggest differences are that Officely focuses on Slack-first
        workplace coordination and hybrid workplace management, while Skedular extends into coworking operations, subscriptions, billing, invoicing,
        marketplace publishing, workspace discovery, and workspace commerce.
      </p>
    ) : isEnvoy ? (
      <p>
        Both platforms support workplace booking and workplace management workflows. The biggest differences are that Envoy focuses on visitor
        management, workplace experience, and workplace operations, while Skedular extends into coworking operations, subscriptions, billing,
        invoicing, marketplace publishing, workspace discovery, and workspace commerce.
      </p>
    ) : isKadence ? (
      <p>
        Both platforms support workplace booking and workplace management workflows. The biggest differences are that Kadence focuses on hybrid
        workplace management, office attendance coordination, and workplace analytics, while Skedular extends into coworking operations,
        subscriptions, billing, invoicing, marketplace publishing, workspace discovery, and workspace commerce.
      </p>
    ) : isArchie ? (
      <p>
        Both platforms support coworking operations and workspace booking workflows. The biggest differences are that Archie focuses on coworking
        administration, memberships, billing, invoicing, and workspace operations, while Skedular extends into marketplace publishing, workspace
        discovery, private workplace management, and workspace commerce.
      </p>
    ) : isDiskbird ? (
      <p>
        Both platforms support workplace booking and workplace management workflows. The biggest differences are that deskbird focuses on hybrid
        workplace management, attendance coordination, workplace visibility, and workplace analytics, while Skedular extends into coworking
        operations, subscriptions, billing, invoicing, marketplace publishing, workspace discovery, and workspace commerce.
      </p>
    ) : (
      <p>
        This table compares known support states from the shared comparison dataset. “Needs review” means the current dataset does not have enough
        approved evidence to make a stronger claim.
      </p>
    )
  }
  <div class="comparison-table-wrap">
    <table class="comparison-feature-table">
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th scope="col">Capability</th>
          <th scope="col">Skedular</th>
          <th scope="col">{competitorName}</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        {
          visibleFeatureRows.map(
            (row) =>
              row && (
                <tr>
                  <th scope="row">
                    <span>{row.feature.name}</span>
                    <small>{row.feature.description}</small>
                  </th>
                  <td>
                    <span class:list={["comparison-support", supportClasses[row.skedularState]]}>
                      {"skedularLabel" in row && row.skedularLabel ? row.skedularLabel : supportLabels[row.skedularState]}
                    </span>
                    {"skedularNote" in row && row.skedularNote && <small>{row.skedularNote}</small>}
                  </td>
                  <td>
                    <span class:list={["comparison-support", supportClasses[row.competitorState]]}>{supportLabels[row.competitorState]}</span>
                    {row.competitorNote && <small>{row.competitorNote}</small>}
                  </td>
                </tr>
              ),
          )
        }
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="comparison-decision-grid" aria-label="Decision guidance">
  <article>
    <h2>Choose Skedular if</h2>
    <ul>
      {skedularUseCases.map((item) => <li>{item}</li>)}
    </ul>
  </article>
  <article>
    <h2>Choose {competitorName} if</h2>
    <ul>
      {
        formatList(
          visibleCompetitorUseCases,
          `Your requirements fit a ${competitorCategory} product and you do not need broader workspace commerce workflows.`,
        ).map((item) => <li>{item}</li>)
      }
    </ul>
  </article>
</section>

<section class="comparison-section" aria-labelledby="key-differences-title">
  <h2 id="key-differences-title">Key differences</h2>
  <div class="comparison-difference-grid">
    {
      visibleDifferenceCards.map((card) => (
        <article>
          <h3>{card.title}</h3>
          <p>{card.body}</p>
        </article>
      ))
    }
  </div>
</section>

<section class="comparison-section">
  <h2>Comparison FAQ</h2>
  <div class="faq-list">
    {
      isSkedda ? (
        <>
          <div class="faq-item">
            <h3>What is the difference between Skedular and Skedda?</h3>
            <p>
              Skedda is strongest as a workplace booking and space management platform for desks, rooms, floor plans, booking rules, permissions, and
              workplace coordination. Skedular is broader across workplace booking, coworking operations, workspace commerce, subscriptions, billing,
              invoicing, marketplace publishing, and public workspace discovery.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="faq-item">
            <h3>Does Skedda support floor plans?</h3>
            <p>Yes. Interactive floor plans are one of Skedda's core strengths.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="faq-item">
            <h3>Does Skedda support Microsoft Teams?</h3>
            <p>
              Yes. Skedda supports Microsoft Teams. Users can book desks from Teams, access floor plans, receive booking notifications, see who is
              coming into the office, and receive visitor notifications when visitor management is enabled.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="faq-item">
            <h3>Does Skedda support Slack?</h3>
            <p>
              Yes. Skedda supports Slack for booking notifications, check-in reminders, visitor notifications, attendance visibility, and recurring
              reports showing who is coming into the office.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="faq-item">
            <h3>Does Skedda support billing and invoicing?</h3>
            <p>
              Partially. Skedda/AllBooked supports Stripe-based booking payments and invoicing for unpaid bookings. Buyers should compare whether they
              need simple booking payment workflows or a broader workspace commerce, billing, invoicing, and accounting workflow.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="faq-item">
            <h3>Does Skedda support subscriptions?</h3>
            <p>
              Partially. Skedda/AllBooked supports membership tags connected to Stripe subscriptions. This can support membership access and recurring
              membership payments, but it should not be described as the same as a broader workspace subscription product model unless the exact buyer
              workflow matches that structure.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="faq-item">
            <h3>Does Skedda support Stripe?</h3>
            <p>Yes. Skedda/AllBooked supports online payments through Stripe and Stripe Connect.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="faq-item">
            <h3>Does Skedda support Xero?</h3>
            <p>
              Partially. Skedda lists Xero as a third-party finance integration. Buyers should compare whether that integration is sufficient for
              their accounting workflow.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="faq-item">
            <h3>Does Skedda have an API?</h3>
            <p>
              Partially. Skedda supports Zapier and webhooks, but Skedda support states that there is currently no open API and that integrations are
              one-way from Skedda to external apps.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="faq-item">
            <h3>Can Skedda be used by coworking spaces?</h3>
            <p>
              Yes. Skedda can support coworking and shared workspace environments, especially where the primary requirements are booking, floor plans,
              resource scheduling, permissions, and payments. Coworking operators that need deeper workspace commerce, marketplace publishing,
              subscriptions, invoicing, and operator workflows should compare the products carefully.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="faq-item">
            <h3>Is Skedda a coworking management platform?</h3>
            <p>
              Skedda can support coworking and shared workspace environments, particularly for booking desks, rooms, and shared resources.
              Organizations requiring broader coworking operations such as subscriptions, invoicing, workspace commerce, marketplace publishing, and
              operator workflows may compare it with platforms designed specifically for coworking management.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="faq-item">
            <h3>Does Skedda support marketplace publishing?</h3>
            <p>
              No. Skedda can be embedded into an existing website for customer-facing booking, but that is different from operating a public workspace
              marketplace or discovery network.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="faq-item">
            <h3>Which platform is better for private organizations?</h3>
            <p>
              Skedda is a strong fit for private organizations that mainly need desk booking, meeting room booking, floor plans, workplace scheduling,
              visitor management, and workplace coordination. Skedular is broader when private workplace workflows also need to connect to coworking
              operations, billing, subscriptions, workspace products, marketplace publishing, or operator workflows.
            </p>
          </div>
          <p class="comparison-review-note">This comparison is based on market research and product documentation available in June 2026.</p>
        </>
      ) : isOfficeRnD ? (
        <>
          <div class="faq-item">
            <h3>What is the difference between Skedular and OfficeRnD?</h3>
            <p>
              OfficeRnD separates workplace management and coworking operations into Workplace and Flex products. Skedular combines workplace booking,
              coworking operations, subscriptions, billing, invoicing, workspace commerce, marketplace publishing, and public workspace discovery in a
              single platform.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="faq-item">
            <h3>Which platform supports subscriptions and billing?</h3>
            <p>
              Both platforms support subscriptions, billing, invoicing, and payment workflows. OfficeRnD provides these capabilities primarily through
              OfficeRnD Flex, while Skedular includes them within its unified platform.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="faq-item">
            <h3>Does OfficeRnD support coworking spaces?</h3>
            <p>Yes. OfficeRnD Flex is specifically designed for coworking and flexible workspace operators.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="faq-item">
            <h3>Does OfficeRnD support billing and invoicing?</h3>
            <p>Yes. OfficeRnD Flex includes recurring billing, invoicing, memberships, contracts, and subscription workflows.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="faq-item">
            <h3>Does OfficeRnD support desk booking?</h3>
            <p>Yes. OfficeRnD Workplace supports desk booking, room booking, floor plans, workplace coordination, and hybrid work workflows.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="faq-item">
            <h3>Does OfficeRnD support Microsoft Teams?</h3>
            <p>Yes. OfficeRnD supports Microsoft Teams and enterprise workplace integrations.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="faq-item">
            <h3>What is the difference between OfficeRnD Workplace and OfficeRnD Flex?</h3>
            <p>
              OfficeRnD Workplace focuses on hybrid workplace management, desk booking, room booking, analytics, and workplace coordination. OfficeRnD
              Flex focuses on coworking operations, memberships, contracts, subscriptions, billing, invoicing, and workspace administration.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="faq-item">
            <h3>Does OfficeRnD support marketplace publishing?</h3>
            <p>
              No. OfficeRnD is not positioned as a public workspace marketplace. Skedular includes public listings, workspace discovery, public
              booking experiences, and marketplace workflows.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="faq-item">
            <h3>Which platform is better for private organizations?</h3>
            <p>
              OfficeRnD is a strong fit for private organizations focused on hybrid workplace management, desk booking, room booking, floor plans,
              workplace analytics, and workplace coordination. Skedular is broader when those workflows also need marketplace publishing, workspace
              discovery, commerce, billing, and operator workflows in one platform.
            </p>
          </div>
          <p class="comparison-review-note">This comparison is based on market research and product documentation available in June 2026.</p>
        </>
      ) : isNexudus ? (
        <>
          <div class="faq-item">
            <h3>Does Nexudus support coworking spaces?</h3>
            <p>Yes. Nexudus is specifically designed for coworking and flexible workspace operators.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="faq-item">
            <h3>Does Nexudus support billing and invoicing?</h3>
            <p>Yes. Nexudus supports recurring billing, invoicing, memberships, contracts, and workspace payments.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="faq-item">
